[Opening "English Opening: King's English Variation, Kramnik-Shirov Counterattack"]

{English Opening: King's English Variation, Kramnik-Shirov Counterattack. A slight inaccuracy in move order — the bishop is better placed before this pawn commits.}
1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 Bb4 3. d3 Nf6 4. Nf3 e4 5. dxe4 Nxe4 {Book so far. The plan is the usual one: finish development, then decide which side to open.} 6. Qd4 Nxc3 7. Bd2 O-O 8. Bxc3 ! Bxc3+ {Prophylaxis. The move looks slow, and it takes away every active idea the opponent had.} (8... Ba3 Rb1 Bxb2 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Qxc3 Nc6 10. e3 d6 11. Bd3 Re8 ?! 12. O-O a5 13. b3 Ne5 14. Nd4 Nxd3 15. Qxd3 Bd7 16. Ne2 Bc6 17. Nc3 Qd7 18. Nd5 Re5 19. Rfd1 h6 20. h3 Rae8 21. Rac1 b6 22. Qc2 Bb7 23. Qc3 f5 24. Rd3 Qf7 25. Rcd1 Kh7 26. Rd4 Rg8 27. a3 Ra8 28. Nf4 Be4 29. b4 Rae8 30. Rc1 Bb7 31. Kh2 Ra8 32. Nd3 Qg6 33. Rg1 Re7 34. Nf4 Qf6 35. Rc1 Re5 36. Qd2 Bc6 37. Kg1 Ra7 38. Nd5 Qf7 39. b5 Bb7 40. Qc2 Ra8 41. a4 Rf8 42. Rcd1 Kg8 43. R1d2 Rb8 44. Rf4 Rf8 45. Rf3 g5 46. Rd4 Qg7 47. Rg3 Rf7 48. Qd1 Bxd5 49. cxd5 Rfe7 50. Qh5 Qf6 51. Rh4 Rg7 52. Qxh6 Qxh6 53. Rxh6 Rxd5 54. Rf3 g4 55. Rf4 g3 56. fxg3 Rxg3 57. Kf2 Rg7 58. g3 Rd2+ 59. Kf3 Rd1 60. Kg2 Rd3 61. Re6 Kf7 62. Ree4 Kg6 63. Re8 Kf7 64. Ree4 Kg6 65. Re8 Kf7 66. Rc8 Ke6 67. Rf8 Rd2+ 68. Kf3 Rd5 69. h4 Rc5 70. Kg2 Re5 71. Kh3 Rh7 72. Re8+ Kf6 73. Rxe5 Kxe5 74. Kg2 d5 75. Kf2 Rh8 76. Ke2 Rh7 77. Rf1 Rg7 78. Kf3 Rg4 79. h5 Kf6 80. Rh1 Kg7 81. Rh4 Rc4 82. Rd4 Rb4 83. Kf4 Kf6 84. h6 Rb1 85. Kf3 Kg6 86. Rh4 Kh7 87. Kf4 c5 88. bxc6 Rc1 89. Kxf5 Rxc6 90. g4 Rc5 91. Ke5 Rc4 92. Kxd5 Rxa4 93. e4 Ra2 94. g5 Rd2+ 95. Ke6 Rg2 96. e5 b5 97. Kf5 b4 98. Rd4 Rf2+ 99. Ke6 Kg6 100. Rd8 a4 101. Rg8+ Kh7 102. Rg7+ Kh8 103. Rd7 a3 104. g6 Kg8 105. h7+ Kh8 106. Rd8+ Rf8 107. Rxf8+ Kg7 108. h8=Q+ Kxg6 {The rest is technique, which is another way of saying it still has to be played accurately.} 109. Rg8# 1-0

[Event "Rook endings - Lucena and Philidor: Chapter 2"]
[ChapterName "The critical sideline"]
