[Opening "Queen's Indian Defense: Spassky System"]

{Queen's Indian Defense: Spassky System. Book so far. The plan is the usual one: finish development, then decide which side to open.}
1. e3 Nf6 2. d4 b6 3. Nf3 e6 4. c4 d5 5. Nc3 Bd6 {A slight inaccuracy in move order — the bishop is better placed before this pawn commits.} 6. b3 O-O 7. h3 Nbd7 8. Be2 ! Ne4 {A long think. Both continuations are playable; this one keeps more pieces on, which suits the attacker.} (8... dxc4 Rb1 cxb3 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Bb2 Nxc3 10. Bxc3 Bb7 11. O-O Qe7 ?! 12. Bb2 f5 13. Qc2 a5 14. Rac1 Kh8 15. c5 bxc5 16. Ba3 c6 17. dxc5 Bb8 18. Nd4 Qf6 19. Nb5 Ba6 20. Nd6 Bxe2 21. Qxe2 h6 22. Bb2 Qe7 23. Qc2 Kh7 24. Rfe1 Ra6 25. Qd3 Ra7 26. Qc2 Kg8 27. Re2 Ra6 28. Ba3 Bc7 29. f3 Bb8 30. Qc3 Qf6 31. Qd3 Ra7 32. f4 Qh4 33. Kh2 Nf6 34. g3 Qh5 35. Bb2 Ng4+ 36. Kg2 Nf6 37. Kh2 Ng4+ 38. Kg2 Nf6 39. Rec2 Ne4 40. Kh2 Qf3 41. Rg2 h5 42. Bd4 h4 43. Rcg1 Nxg3 44. Qc2 Qh5 45. Rxg3 hxg3+ 46. Rxg3 Kh7 47. Rg5 Qh4 48. Qg2 Qh6 49. Qe2 g6 50. h4 Qxh4+ 51. Kg1 Qh3 52. Rg2 Kg8 53. Rh2 Qg3+ 54. Rg2 Qh3 55. Qf1 Qh5 56. Rh2 Qg4+ 57. Rg2 Qh4 58. Rh2 Qg3+ 59. Rg2 Qh4 60. Rxg6+ Kh7 61. Qg2 Qe1+ 62. Kh2 Qh4+ 63. Kg1 Qe1+ 64. Kh2 Qh4+ {Precise to the end. A pawn move here instead would have let the defence build a fortress.} 65. Kg1 1/2-1/2
